### nix-init
.direnv
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# ROOT-LAYER ONLY — do NOT cascade this line to a descendant.
#
# The root deliberately has NO committed lock: its flake.nix pins every input to
# an exact commit, so a lock is a second copy of the same fact that can disagree
# with the first. But nix WRITES the lock on every evaluation and `git add` picks
# it up, so the absence has to be enforced rather than merely intended.
#
# `workspace` and everything below it DO commit a lock, and their pin gate reads
# it as a second copy that must agree with flake.nix. Inheriting this line there
# would contradict their own law, so a merge from the root drops it.
flake.lock
